<title>USA: Barr Labs board sets 3-for-2 stock split.</title>
<headline>Barr Labs board sets 3-for-2 stock split.</headline>
<dateline>POMONA, N.Y. 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Barr Laboratories Inc said Monday that in recognition of the potential ongoing contribution of the settlement of a patent case with Bayer AG in a patent case, it has approved a 3-for-2 stock split to be effected in the form of a 50 percent stock dividend.</p>
<p>The dividend will be payable May 7 to shareholders of record April 24.</p>
<p>The company said that under the terms of the settlement with Bayer in the ciprofloxacin patent case, which was announced in January, it will receive  an initial cash payment of $24.6 million, and signed a contingent, non-exclusive Supply Agreement that has a potential value similar to that received in 1997 for the next six years.</p>
<p>The company said it was also splitting its stock in recognition of the pending launch of Barr's Warfarin Sodium anti-coagulant.</p>
